ode on the outside and everything else is at least two layers deeper. Also, for some reason you have a Structural Node on the front lines despite there being no benefit for doing so unless you intend to use it for conspiracy actions (which it will universally make at a penalty because Structural Nodes are not suited for Power or Finesse).<br /> <br /> If the map is instead meant to treat the outside edges of the chart as the perimeter, you have the bigger problem of giving a Hierarchical Node no screen against investigation; also, as with the previous one, having three Hierarchical Nodes is a potential liability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}